+# Pilot: Fairness, Privacy & HIL Safety — Runbook
+
+Purpose
+- Execute an integrated pilot that (1) reduces model bias via domain randomization and active learning, (2) ensures medical data privacy with Vault+retrieval guard, (3) enforces HIL gates for competition actions, (4) uses secure aggregation for federated updates, and (5) runs Gatekeeper audit → enforcement safely.
+
+Prerequisites
+- Vault HA deployed and transit key created
+- Rekor deployed and receipt_signer configured
+- Milvus running for active learning
+- A2A service deployed and reachable
+- Gatekeeper installed and constraints created in dry-run
+- Prometheus & Alertmanager deployed and oncall configured
+
+Steps
+1. Fairness augmentation
+   - Generate synthetic data: python services/simulation/domain_randomization_enhanced.py --n 5000 --out synth.jsonl --balance "gender:0.4"
+   - Merge with real labeled data; run cross-validation and fairness audit: python services/fairness/fairness_audit.py --data merged.csv --sensitive impairment
+   - If disparities found, add targeted synthetic examples and active learn from edge_case_sampler results.
+
+2. Active learning loop
+   - Run sampler: python services/active_learning/edge_case_sampler.py --k 100
+   - Present samples to annotators via the annotation UI; post annotations to active_loop_api.
+   - Retrain models with curated labels and re-run fairness audit.
+
+3. Privacy & retrieval guard
+   - Ensure consent is recorded with consent_manager_optout for medical scope.
+   - For any original retrieval, use retrieval_guard_audit.retrieve_original and require HIL approval via A2A service.
+   - Check MCP audit endpoint to verify retrieval events are recorded.
+
+4. HIL enforcement for competition actions
+   - All automated recommendations must call require_hil_enforcer.intent prior to executing any action.
+   - During competition, prefer fetchtoken offline approvals and local redemption; sync redemption events to MCP.
+
+5. Secure aggregation for federated rounds
+   - Use secure_aggregation prototype only for integration testing; for production switch to vetted library.
+   - Enforce policy via secureagg/policy_enforcer to require group size >= 3 and enrollment tokens (Vault-issued).
+
+6. Gatekeeper audit → enforcement
+   - Run gatekeeper audit cron (gatekeeper-audit-cronjob) for 48–72 hours; monitor violations in MCP.
+   - Use tools/auto_gatekeeper_flip.sh CronJob to flip enforcement only if violations < threshold and operator reviewed.
+
+7. Post-runbook actions
+   - Produce fairness report, consent/access logs, HIL evidence receipts, and secure aggregation summary; upload to MCP for governance review.
+   - If any policy violations or privacy concerns, pause promotion to production until remediated.
+
